  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 4,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.046,
            0.347,
            0.063
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.088,
            0.848,
            0.127
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The expression 4m + 2q will always evaluate to an even number for any integer values of m and q. We can justify this in two different ways —"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.131,
            0.846,
            0.169
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We know 4m is even and 2q is even for any integers m and q. Therefore, their sum will also be even."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.173,
            0.848,
            0.249
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The expression "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 m \\pm 2 q"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is equal to the expression "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 ( 2 m + q )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Here, the expression "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 ( 2 m + q )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " means 2 times "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 m + q ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " In other words, 2 is a factor of this expression. Therefore, this expression will always give an even number for any integers m and q."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.253,
            0.847,
            0.29
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For example, if m = 4 and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "q = - 9 ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , the expression 4m + 2q becomes "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 \\times 4 + 2 \\times ( - 9) = - 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , which is an even number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.289,
            0.848,
            0.364
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the expression x"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " + 2, x"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is even if x is even, and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is odd if x is odd. Therefore, the expression "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x ^ { 2 }   +   2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " will "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "not",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " always give an even number. An example and a non-example for when the expression evaluates to an even number — (i) if x = 6, then "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x ^ { 2 } + 2 = 3 8"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and (ii) if x = 3, then "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x^{2} + 2 = 11."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.371,
            0.848,
            0.431
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Similarly, determine and explain which of the other expressions always give even numbers. Write a couple of examples and non-examples, as appropriate, for each expression."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.444,
            0.836,
            0.467
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Write a few algebraic expressions which always give an even number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.486,
            0.395,
            0.507
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pairs to Make Fours"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.523,
            0.791,
            0.545
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Take a pair of even numbers. Add them. Is the sum divisible by 4?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.547,
            0.606,
            0.566
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Try this with different pairs of even numbers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.566,
            0.658,
            0.585
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When is the sum a multiple of 4, and when is it not?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.585,
            0.503,
            0.603
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Is there a general rule or a pattern?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.602,
            0.847,
            0.641
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Even numbers can be of two types based on the remainders they leave when divided by 4."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.228,
            0.674,
            0.393,
            0.798
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 14,
              "bbox": [
                0.228,
                0.674,
                0.393,
                0.798
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_4_image_14.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_footnote",
              "index": 15,
              "bbox": [
                0.185,
                0.808,
                0.441,
                0.851
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Even numbers that are multiples of 4 leave a remainder of 0 when divided by 4."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.597,
            0.681,
            0.755,
            0.797
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 16,
              "bbox": [
                0.597,
                0.681,
                0.755,
                0.797
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_4_image_16.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_footnote",
              "index": 17,
              "bbox": [
                0.548,
                0.808,
                0.803,
                0.85
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Even numbers that are not multiples of 4 leave a remainder 2 when divided by 4."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
